<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak.xml    RimUtinni Patches · FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1

  Wires the F2 spike class (RUT_IncidentWorker_MirrorBreak, compiling and
  proven `src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/`) into a real,
  reachable IncidentDef — the_fever_wood.md §4/§8's "a ripple crosses a
  mirror that nothing touched": "a rare event on a random registered pool"
  (fever_wood_kit_spec.md F2).

  MayRequire is load-bearing: mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards ships the
  class this workerClass names. Without the gate a mod list missing that
  mod would discard this def silently (memory:
  modextension-missing-type-discards-def) rather than erroring loudly.

  Safe everywhere, not just the Fever Wood: RUT_IncidentWorker_MirrorBreak's
  own TryExecuteWorker returns false (a silent no-op, never an error) on any
  map with no terrain carrying RM_LurkingWaterExtension — which, pending the
  donor terrain audit this item's spike pass flagged as owed (no vendored
  COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Tropical terrain defs in this repo to safely name),
  is every map today. The def is real and reachable by the storyteller now;
  it starts doing anything the moment F1's terrain-side hookup lands.

  baseChance/minRefireDays: INVENTED tuning (kit spec's own vocabulary),
  scaled down from RUT_FlameHarvest's baseChance 4 (RUT_PyrelandsIncidents.xml)
  to match F2's own framing, "rare event" — an atmosphere beat, not a threat.
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak</defName>
    <label>mirror break</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_IncidentWorker_MirrorBreak</workerClass>
    <baseChance>1.2</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>8</minRefireDays>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
